      "content": "i get that it's hard to map perfectly, but we don't have time for massive ablation studies. we need to be surgical. if we don't strip the specialized layers, the reviewers will just say the result is a \"black box\" fluke. can you at least pinpoint the layers where the topological phase heuristics are most dense? i need to know which ones are 'essential' to the discovery so i can try to preserve them while still satisfying the peer-review requirement for a lighter model.",
